{{wikipedia}}
==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# {{countable}} (mostly in botany and forestry) The [[wood]] from any [[dicotyledon]]ous tree, without regard to its hardness.
#: {{usex|Balsa is a '''hardwood''', but a soft hardwood.}}
# {{countable}} (in more general use) As the preceding but limited to those that are commercial [[timber]]s, and are at least average in hardness.
#: {{usex|Ash, hickory and oak are some of the most prominent domestic '''hardwoods'''.}}
# {{countable|forestry}} The tree or tree species that yields the preceding.
#: {{usex|This '''hardwood''' has been planted extensively throughout the hills here.}}
# {{uncountable}} A joint term for the commercial timbers, without distinguishing which.
#: {{usex|You should have used '''hardwood''' for this window sill instead of this junk.}}

